<title>USA: PAKISTAN GETS $25 MLN MORE IN USDA EXPORT CREDITS.</title>
<headline>PAKISTAN GETS $25 MLN MORE IN USDA EXPORT CREDITS.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department on Thursday boosted Pakistan's allocation to buy wheat and other commodities under the fiscal 1997 GSM-102 export credit program by $25 million.</p>
<p>The action bring's Pakistan's total allocation for the year to $350 million.</p>
<p>((Washington commodities desk 202 898 8341))</p>
</text>
